Third-party code in src/port/armv4t
===================================

This folder is for any 32-bit Arm with ARM state, from Armv4T on, in either
byte order: ARM7TDMI, the ARM9 family (ARM920T is Armv4T, ARM926EJ-S and
ARM946E-S are Armv5TE), ARM11, and Cortex-R and Cortex-A cores. It is the
folder for TI's TMS570, whose Cortex-R4F and R5F run big-endian, and for its
RM4x, which run little-endian. src/port/arm needs Armv7-A in little-endian
order, and its memset.S declares .arch armv7-a, which GNU ld refuses to
link with R-profile objects.

Four files below come from musl and newlib, copied byte for byte and never
edited. They keep their names and their notices. The other files are
libterae's own and carry libterae's notice: port_memcpy.S, port_memmove.S,
port_aeabi_memcpy.S and port_aeabi_memset.S, which are the files assembled,
and port_memset.c and port_memcmp.c.

memcpy.S and aeabi_memmove-arm.S carry the full text of their licences.
musl's two __aeabi files carry no notice, and musl's COPYRIGHT, reproduced at
the end of this file, puts such files under its MIT licence.


